.TH ZSTD-SPLITTER 1 "2026-07-28" "zstd-splitter 4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zstd-splitter \- tar compression, splitting, integrity, and SSH/SFTP transfer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zstd-splitter
-c -s SIZE [options] SOURCE
.br
.B zstd-splitter
-j|-x|-v [options] INPUT
.br
.B zstd-splitter
-P -i -R DESTINATION [network-options] INPUT
.br
.B zstd-splitter
-G -i -R REMOTE_INPUT [network-options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Version 4.0 is a POSIX /bin/sh release at feature level 40. It preserves the strict manifest format inherited from 3.0 and publishes local and remote output only after validation.
.SH ACTIONS AND OPTIONS
.TP
.B -c
Create, compress, and split a tar stream.
.TP
.B -j
Join parts and verify the archive.
.TP
.B -x
Extract a verified archive or part set.
.TP
.B -v
Verify without extraction.
.TP
.B -P
Push through SSH/SFTP.
.TP
.B -G
Pull and verify through SSH/SFTP.
.TP
.B -Q MODE
Query network or config.
.TP
.B -E
List compression engines.
.TP
.B -i
Enable strict SHA-256 processing.
.TP
.B -m MANIFEST
Use an explicit manifest.
.TP
.B -d DIRECTORY
Set extraction or pull destination.
.TP
.B -f
Permit replacement or destructive maintenance.
.TP
.B -R SPEC
Set [user@]host:/absolute/path.
.TP
.B -O NAME=VALUE
Set a network option; repeatable.
.TP
.B -F FILE
Read network options from a file.
.TP
.B -h
Display help.
.SH NETWORK MODEL
One effective destination is accepted. Push and pull use staging, retries, verification, optional locks, optional remote extraction, and atomic publication.
.PP
Detailed NAME=VALUE settings are documented in docs/NETWORK-OPTIONS.md in the source package.
.SH STRICT INTEGRITY
Strict mode records and validates the canonical source inventory, whole compressed archive, each split part, and restored content. SHA-256 provides integrity, not origin authentication.
.SH PORTABILITY
This feature release uses the GNU-oriented dependency profile. The matching .1 maintenance release adds macOS/BSD utility abstraction without changing feature level.
.SH SECURITY
Host-key checking defaults to strict. Temporary state is private. Archive extraction and publication are transactional. Protect SSH keys, known_hosts, manifests, parent directories, and resource limits. See docs/RUNTIME-SECURITY.md.
.SH DOCUMENTATION
README.md is the entry point. docs/INDEX.md routes to exact protocol, security, architecture, portability, and test documents. Code comments follow EIGIIB and state rationale rather than line-by-line mechanics.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Operational, integrity, file, or network failure.
.TP
.B 2
Usage, configuration, or feature-gate error.
.TP
.B 128+N
Termination by signal N.
.SH FILES
.I /usr/local/bin/zstd-splitter
.br
.I /usr/local/share/man/man1/zstd-splitter.1.gz
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssh (1),
.BR sftp (1),
.BR tar (1)
